__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=3&visit=6", "\"Do you know Maury Stark?\" you ask.<p>\"Maury Stark is less a person, and more a sort of angry vole,\" Addison says. \"That twitching nose, those beady little eyes... Go have a look in the Smoking Lounge, Detective -- you'll find the resemblance positively uncanny!\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=rel&w=3&visit=6", "\"What can you tell me about the deceased's housekeeper?\" you ask.<p>\"Oh, him,\" Addison says with a slight grimace. \"That little blighter goes by the name Maury Stark, Detective. Nasty piece of work. Face like a horse. And I shall leave the question of which bit of the horse to your own deductive prowess.\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=3&visit=6", "\"Do you know Maury Stark?\" you ask.<p>\"Well, there's nothing like a good friend, Detective,\" Addison says, \"and that creature currently residing within the Smoking Lounge is nothing like a good friend!\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=rel&w=3&visit=6", "\"The victim had a housekeeper, do you know them?\" you ask.<p>\"Oh, him,\" Addison says with a slight grimace. \"That little blighter goes by the name Maury Stark, Detective. Nasty piece of work. Face like a horse. And I shall leave the question of which bit of the horse to your own deductive prowess.\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=3&visit=6", "\"Do you know someone by the name of Maury Stark?\" you ask.<p>\"I stay bloody well away from that character, Detective,\" Addison says, \"if you'll excuse the 'bloody'. Could set your hat alight with a glare, he could. He's in the Smoking Lounge, go see for yourself!\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=rel&w=3&visit=6", "\"What can you tell me about the deceased's housekeeper?\" you ask.<p>\"Oh, that's a rotten one there, Detective,\" Addison says. \"Calls himself 'Maury Stark', but is that even his legitimate moniker? ... ...Well, yes, probably. Can't quite imagine someone calling themselves 'Maury Stark' by choice, can you?\""));
