__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=rel&w=6&visit=7", "\"Do you know Rocha's gardener?\" you ask.<p>\"Oh yes! Yes, quite well,\" Stevie says. \"What was the name... hmm... Began with an S, I believe. Or an R? ...No, it's no good, I'm afraid, old chap. You'll have to go to the Basement and ask for yourself.\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=6&visit=7", "\"Are you familiar with a man named Stephen Thomas?\" you ask.<p>\"Oh yes, Stephen Thomas's a positive delight!\" Stevie says. \"Why, I could tell you some real stories, Detective!\"<p>\"That won't be necessary,\" you say. <p>\"Just as well. I'd forgotten you were a policeman for a moment.\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=rel&w=6&visit=7", "\"I understand the victim had a gardener,\" you say. \"Can you tell me anything about them?\"<p>\"Oh certainly, certainly,\" Stevie says. \"Indubitably, even, if I'm correct in assuming that to be a word. Spends a lot of time in the Basement, don't you know. Yes yes, we're quite close.\"<p>\"Do you know their name?\" you ask.<p>\"Haven't the foggiest.\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=6&visit=7", "\"What do you know about Stephen Thomas?\" you ask.<p>\"Certainly!\" Stevie says. \"Marvelous man, just brilliant. He's Mariah's child, did you know that? Wouldn't think it to look at him! But it's like the Greeks said, you know, Detective.\"<p>\"...What did they say?\"<p>\"Hmm? Oh, I don't speak a word of Greek. Something about columns, I expect.\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=rel&w=6&visit=7", "\"Do you know Rocha's gardener?\" you ask.<p>\"Oh certainly, certainly,\" Stevie says. \"Indubitably, even, if I'm correct in assuming that to be a word. Spends a lot of time in the Basement, don't you know. Yes yes, we're quite close.\"<p>\"Do you know their name?\" you ask.<p>\"Haven't the foggiest.\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=6&visit=7", "\"Stephen Thomas. What can you tell me about him?\" you ask.<p>\"Lovely man, Stephen Thomas. Always stands his round, wouldn't say a word against him,\" Stevie says. \"Did you know he's Mariah's child? I was flabbergasted when I found out!\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=rel&w=6&visit=7", "\"Have you met the victim's gardener?\" you ask.<p>\"Why yes, we get along splendidly,\" Stevie says. \"If we're thinking of the same person, that is. With the um? In the Basement? Is that the one?\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=8&visit=7", "\"Manny Sharp. What can you tell me about him?\" you ask.<p>\"Hmm,\" Stevie muses. \"Hmm and also hmm. Oh, steady on, do you mean Old Mariah's personal assistant? Hah! No, Detective -- you'd need to pay me a fair penny just to stand behind him in a queue!\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=rel&w=8&visit=7", "\"The victim's neighbor -- do you know them?\" you ask.<p>\"Oh, that's a rotten one there, Detective,\" Stevie says. \"Calls herself 'Kylie Holder', but is that even her legitimate moniker? ... ...Well, yes, probably. Can't quite imagine someone calling themselves 'Kylie Holder' by choice, can you?\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=8&visit=7", "\"What do you know about Manny Sharp?\" you ask.<p>\"Oh, that scallywag,\" Stevie says. \"He's Mariah's personal assistant, you know -- and a boor, and a bore, and a bounder to boot!\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=rel&w=8&visit=7", "\"What can you tell me about the deceased's neighbor?\" you ask.<p>\"Do you mean Kylie Holder, Detective?\" Stevie asks. \"Well! I'm not one to tell tales out of school, but well. Hmph! Yes. Tch! With perhaps a Hoh! and Tsk! for good measure.\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=8&visit=7", "\"Do you know Manny Sharp?\" you ask.<p>\"Great Scott, do you mean Old Mariah's personal assistant?\" Stevie says. \"Well, here's what I have to say about that particular bounder, Detective: Hmph! And furthermore, tut!\""));
