__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=3&visit=6", "\"What do you know about Sofia Crosby?\" you ask.<p>\"She's in the Basement right now,\" Clayton says, \"but I don't think she did the murder. At least, I haven't found any evidence to suggest it yet!\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=rel&w=3&visit=6", "\"Can you tell me anything about the victim's boss? you ask.<p>\"They're in the Living Room, if I know who you mean, Detective,\" Clayton says. \"We've never really talked or anything.\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=3&visit=6", "\"What do you know about Sofia Crosby?\" you ask.<p>\"Oh sure, Detective! Sofia Crosby's great fun!\" Clayton says. \"She's in the Basement right now. She'll probably share her chewing gum with you, if you ask!\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=rel&w=3&visit=6", "\"What can you tell me about the deceased's boss?\" you ask.<p>\"They seem nice enough, but I've never really talked to them, Detective,\" Clayton says. \"I think they're in the Living Room?\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=3&visit=6", "\"Do you know someone by the name of Sofia Crosby?\" you ask.<p>\"I sure do!\" Clayton says. \"She's in the Basement. I don't think she did it, but it's dangerous to make assumptions before you have all the facts. That's like the first rule of detectiveing!\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=rel&w=3&visit=6", "\"Have you met the victim's boss?\" you ask.<p>\"That must be who's in the Living Room right now, Detective, \"Clayton says. \"I was trying to figure out who that was, we've never really been introduced.\""));
