__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=3&visit=6", "\"Gustav Montoya. What can you tell me about him?\" you ask.<p>\"He's in the Hall Closet right now,\" Clancy says, \"but I don't think he did the murder. At least, I haven't found any evidence to suggest it yet!\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=rel&w=3&visit=6", "\"Have you met the victim's college roommate?\" you ask.<p>\"Uh-huh, that's Harold Munoz. He's pretty funny,\" Clancy says. \"Wait, do you think he did it? Should I be investigating him?\" <p>\"You should be sitting here quietly without investigate anything,\" you say sternly. <p>\"Aw, gee!\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=3&visit=6", "\"Do you know Gustav Montoya?\" you ask.<p>\"He's in the Hall Closet right now,\" Clancy says, \"but I don't think he did the murder. At least, I haven't found any evidence to suggest it yet!\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=rel&w=3&visit=6", "\"Can you tell me anything about the victim's college roommate? you ask.<p>\"Oh sure, that's Harold Munoz. He's real nice! ...Wait, you don't think he did the murder, do you?\" he gasps."));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=3&visit=6", "\"Gustav Montoya. What can you tell me about him?\" you ask.<p>\"Oh sure, Detective! Gustav Montoya's great fun!\" Clancy says. \"He's in the Hall Closet right now. He'll probably share his chewing gum with you, if you ask!\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=rel&w=3&visit=6", "\"I understand the victim had a college roommate,\" you say. \"Can you tell me anything about them?\"<p>\"Oh, you mean Harold Munoz?\" Clancy says. \"I'd be real surprised if he did it, Detective! But I guess you have to cover all the bases in our line of work!\""));
__core_text_test_data.listAppend(listMake("wham.php?ask=3&visit=6", "\"What can you tell me about Gustav Montoya?\" you ask.<p>\"I sure do!\" Clancy says. \"He's in the Hall Closet. I don't think he did it, but it's dangerous to make assumptions before you have all the facts. That's like the first rule of detectiveing!\""));
